Good morning,

We are instructed to notify a theft from the Cypress Landing Data Hall B project. Our reference is SRR/BR/2025/1147.

A note on the policy number below. The client's project team submitted this to us quoting IM-2298-66401, which is their contractors equipment floater, because that is where site inventory is tracked. Their own risk manager does not agree and has set out why in the attached report. Please read her allocation before the file is set up.

Policy number quoted by the client: IM-2298-66401
Broker reference: SRR/BR/2025/1147
Project name: Cypress Landing Data Hall B
Contract number: CONSENSUSDOCS-410-2025-CLB
Insured name: Meridian Grid Holdings, LLC
Contractor: Ironbark Constructors, Inc.
Date of loss: 11 April 2026
Loss location: 14900 South Cypress Landing Way, Mesa, AZ 85212
Estimated loss: USD 1,318,100

Fence fabric was cut on the north-east boundary overnight on Saturday, after two
cameras covering that approach were disabled. They took copper feeder cable off
the reels and out of two duct bank runs, stripped the substation ground ring,
and cut out sixteen busway sections. Two owner-supplied UPS cabinets were
damaged in an attempt to strip them.

About 96% of the value is material staged for installation into the building.
That is permanent works, not contractors equipment, and the equipment floater
excludes it in terms. The welder, the hand tools and the fence are the only part
that belongs on the floater.

The UPS cabinets have not been moved, opened or cleaned and are tagged do not
move pending your inspection.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * risk manager's allocation report
  * loss allocation schedule

Please open this against the project's builder's risk policy and confirm a claim
reference. We will notify the equipment floater separately for the USD 54,100.

